📍 Mozambique | Working across Africa & globally
🧠 About Me

I am a multidisciplinary engineer and researcher with over six years of experience designing scalable applications, data pipelines, and social welfare interventions. My work bridges the gap between software engineering, predictive data science, and macro-level social policy to build high-impact digital infrastructure. 
•	I hold professional certifications in Systems Architecture from IBM and Advanced Data Analytics from Google. 
•	I currently serve as the Southern Africa Regional Focal Point for the SDG7 Youth Constituency, leading regional stakeholder coordination for sustainable energy access. 
•	My technical approach is rooted in evidence-based decision-making, child-centered systems, climate innovation, and ethical, human-centered design.

🛠️ Technical Arsenal
•	Full-Stack Engineering: React.js, Next.js (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS. 
•	Backend & Cloud: Node.js, NestJS, Express.js, REST APIs, GraphQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB. 
•	Data Science & Analytics: Python (Pandas, Scikit-learn), R, SQL, Power BI, Tableau, Predictive Modeling, PACE Framework. 
•	Emerging Tech: Internet Computer Protocol (ICP), Motoko smart contracts, Decentralized application (dApp) design. 

📊 Featured Open-Source & Portfolio Projects
•	HydroNexus One (Digital Public Infrastructure): Spearheaded the deployment of an open-source framework using the MERN stack for transboundary antimicrobial resistance (AMR) data surveillance. Engineered a secure, admin-gated data validation pipeline with an immutable transactional log to guarantee data integrity across jurisdictions. 
•	Automatidata (Machine Learning): Built a regression-based ML model to forecast NYC taxi fares, utilizing the PACE framework for full data lifecycle management. 
•	DBank (DeFi on ICP): Architected a decentralized banking application using Motoko, featuring 1% compound interest logic, stable memory persistence, and Internet Identity integration. 
•	ShopHub (E-commerce SaaS): Engineered a high-performance storefront using Next.js 13, TypeScript, and centralized state management via Zustand.

📄 Research & Advocacy
•	Peer-Reviewed Publication: Digital Health Information Systems and the Management of Child Stunting in Malawi (2026). Published in the International Journal of Innovative Science and Research Technology, this study evaluates how digital health systems improve data-driven decision-making and public welfare outcomes. 
•	Climate & Circular Economy: Piloting Waste to Wealth innovations using Black Soldier Fly (BSF) systems and advancing circular bioeconomy concepts.

